# Once UI codegen harness

Cursor cannot read `node_modules`, so this repo vendors the harness at `.cursor/once-ui-ai/` (copied from `@once-ui-system/core@1.8.4`). Refresh after upgrading the package:

`rsync -a --delete node_modules/@once-ui-system/core/ai/ .cursor/once-ui-ai/`

Before generating or editing Once UI UI code in this project:

1. Read `.cursor/once-ui-ai/manifest.json`
2. Load bootstrap files from the manifest: `rules.compact.md` + `catalog.json`
3. Resolve intent via `.cursor/once-ui-ai/tasks/index.json` → fetch the matching task bundle
4. Fetch only the component slices listed in that task (`.cursor/once-ui-ai/components/*.json`)
5. Read the task's gold example; for production layouts, read matching Pro blocks from `.cursor/once-ui-ai/examples/blocks/manifest.json`
6. Validate output: `npx once-ui-validate-ai-code path/to/file.tsx`

## Do not

- Use full documentation MDX pages for codegen (too large; use the harness)
- Use `Flex direction="column"` when `Column` works; same for `Row`
- Use `fillWidth fillHeight` when `fill` works
- Use `Card` for static panels (use the surface recipe on `Column`)

